## Q3: Chrome Web Store Submission — Full Guide

### Prerequisites
- A **Google developer account** (one-time $5 USD registration fee)
- Your extension as a `.zip` file of the `extension/` folder
- 1-5 screenshots (1280×800 or 640×400 px)
- A small promotional tile image (440×280 px)

### Submission Checklist (Google's Requirements)

| Requirement | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Manifest V3 | ✅ | Already using it |
| No remote code execution | ✅ | All JS is in the package |
| Minimal permissions | ✅ | Only what is needed |
| `geolocation` justification | ✅ | Must explain in Store listing |
| `enterprise.deviceAttributes` justification | ✅ | Must explain in listing |
| Privacy Policy URL | ⬜ | **Required** for any extension requesting sensitive permissions |
| Single purpose | ✅ | Only does location tracking |
| No deceptive practices | ✅ | Installed by IT admin, not end users |

### Step-by-Step Publishing Process

1. Go to the [Chrome Developer Dashboard](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/devconsole)
2. Click **Add new item**.
3. Zip your extension: `Compress the extension/ folder` → `extension.zip`
4. Upload `extension.zip`.
5. Fill in the listing:
   - **Name**: `ChromeOS Location Tracker`
   - **Summary**: Enterprise IT location tracking for managed ChromeOS devices.
   - **Description**: Explain clearly it is an enterprise extension for IT admins, installed via policy.
   - **Category**: `Productivity`
   - **Visibility**: Set to **Unlisted** (only your domain can install it via policy) — this is best practice for enterprise extensions.
6. Under **Privacy**, add a hosted **Privacy Policy URL** explaining what location data is collected, who can see it, and how it's used.
7. Under **Permissions Justification**, explain:
   - `geolocation`: Required to read device GPS coordinates for enterprise IT fleet management.
   - `enterprise.deviceAttributes`: Required to link location data to the correct managed device in the admin portal.
8. Upload screenshots.
9. Submit for review (usually 1-3 business days).

### Google Policy Compliance — Critical Rules
> [!CAUTION]
> Violating these will get your extension **permanently suspended**.

- ✅ **DO** state clearly in the description that this is an enterprise IT extension installed by an admin.
- ✅ **DO** include a hosted Privacy Policy that explains data collection.
- ✅ **DO** use **Unlisted** visibility so it isn't publicly searchable.
- ❌ **DO NOT** collect data from users who have not consented — document the admin-consent flow.
- ❌ **DO NOT** use any obfuscated code.
- ❌ **DO NOT** use `eval()` or load remote scripts.

