## Q5: Automatic/Dynamic Device ID (Already Done!)

The extension already handles this **automatically** on real enrolled ChromeOS devices.

The code in `background.js`:
```js
if (chrome.enterprise && chrome.enterprise.deviceAttributes) {
  deviceId = await new Promise((resolve) => {
    chrome.enterprise.deviceAttributes.getDirectoryDeviceId(resolve);
  });
}
```
- On a **real managed ChromeOS device**: Google's `enterprise.deviceAttributes` API returns the exact Directory Device ID automatically. No manual entry ever needed.
- On a **regular PC** (like your test): This API is not available, so it falls back to `"unknown"` (or your hardcoded test ID). This is **expected** and correct.

**For production**: Simply revert the hardcoded ID back to `"unknown"` on line 21 of `background.js`. The API will take over automatically on enrolled ChromeOS devices.

