## Q6: Prevent Users from Removing the Extension

When you deploy the extension through the **Google Admin Console Policy** (which is exactly what your portal's "Deploy Location Tracker" button does via `FORCE_INSTALLED`), **users cannot remove it**. This is enforced at the OS policy level.

Specifically:
- The extension will have no **"Remove"** button on the `chrome://extensions/` page.
- Even if a user tries via the command line or developer mode, it will be reinstalled at next policy sync.
- It will automatically reinstall if the device is reset and re-enrolled.

The policy you are already sending (`installationType: "FORCE_INSTALLED"`) is precisely the mechanism for this. No extra code is needed — it's built into ChromeOS enterprise policy enforcement.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This enforcement **only works** on managed, enrolled ChromeOS devices in your Google Workspace domain. It does **not** apply to regular Windows/Mac PCs where you are currently testing.
